2.0.0
=====

 * Upgrade bundled jQuery from 1.2.6 to 4.0.0 (full browser build), fixing
   CVE-2011-4969 and incorporating subsequent upstream security fixes.
   Source and checksum: lib/wparts-2.0.0/priv/JQUERY.md.
 * Adapt autocomplete to the supported jQuery APIs and correct lookupLocal()
   to access the autocomplete instance on the input element. Preserve plugin
   entry points, options, callbacks, CSS classes and suggestion formatting.
 * Bump eptic, wpart and wparts together to 2.0.0. This is a major release
   because applications using the bundled jQuery may need JavaScript changes
   and legacy browsers are no longer supported. Erlang APIs are unchanged.

 * wpart_my_primitive_type:load_tpl() is called automatically for
   all user-defined primitive types on application startup.
   - you don't have to do it yourself anymore
   - make sure that you implement load_tpl
     (it's required by wpart behaviour, anyway)

Migration from 1.x
-----------------

1. Install the eptic-2.0.0, wpart-2.0.0 and wparts-2.0.0 directories together.
   Update application-specific build/include paths and release specifications;
   remove superseded framework directories from the runtime code path. Rebuild
   the application and regenerate its boot/release files. Separately versioned
   dependencies and the generated application's own version are unchanged.
2. Review application-owned JavaScript and other plugins against the jQuery
   upgrade guides, including intermediate releases:
   https://jquery.com/upgrade-guide/
   Removed APIs include $.browser, .size() and $.trim. Attribute/property,
   selector, ready-handler and AJAX behavior have also changed since 1.2.6.
   Migrate can be used temporarily while diagnosing application code, following
   the upstream staged upgrade instructions; it is not bundled or required by
   Erlang Web. Do not deploy intermediate vulnerable jQuery versions.
3. Back up customized assets, then replace BOTH docroot/jquery.js and
   docroot/jquery.autocomplete.js with their counterparts from
   lib/wparts-2.0.0/priv/. Merge any local autocomplete customizations into the
   updated plugin before deployment. Preserve script order: jQuery, plugin,
   application initialization. Refresh any copied/customized autocomplete.tpl
   from lib/wparts-2.0.0/priv/html/ and restart to reload framework templates.
4. Deploy the paired assets together and invalidate browser/proxy/CDN caches
   (or update asset cache keys). Check the served jQuery.fn.jquery is 4.0.0 and
   exercise application autocomplete. bin/start.erl intentionally skips files
   already present in docroot: rerunning setup alone does NOT upgrade them.

Browser requirements follow jQuery 4.0:
https://jquery.com/upgrade-guide/4.0/#browser-support
IE 11; current and previous Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari; current Opera;
current and two previous iOS Safari releases; current and previous Android.
IE 10 and older and legacy Edge are no longer supported.

Suggestion formatting still accepts trusted HTML, including formatItem output.
This dependency upgrade does not make untrusted suggestion HTML safe.

